---
import '../../styles/kit.css';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import { href, pageMeta } from '../../lib/site';
import { docsArticle, docsBreadcrumbs } from '../../lib/jsonld';
const h1 = "Security";
---

<Page path="/docs/security" ogType="article" jsonLd={[docsArticle(h1, pageMeta('/docs/security').description, '/docs/security'), docsBreadcrumbs(h1, '/docs/security')]}>
	<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	    <div class="bd first"><div class="wrap"><h1 class="t60">Security</h1></div></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="s0" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="s0" class="t28">Read this before you point it at a site</h2></div>
	<p>a11ign drives a real browser and a real screen reader on a page you name. It doesn’t just look. It operates controls the way a user would, so know what it touches.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="s1" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="s1" class="t28">What it does to a page</h2></div>
	<ul class="grid"><li><Card title="Opens disclosures, such as menus and drop-downs">Always. Opening something has no side effects.</Card></li><li><Card title="Follows the first link on the page">By default. It’s usually the skip link. Turn it off with --no-probe-navigation.</Card></li><li><Card title="Submits forms and presses buttons">Only if you turn on probe-forms. It’s off by default.</Card></li><li><Card title="Ticks checkboxes and radio buttons">Only with probe-forms on.</Card></li><li><Card title="Types values you wrote into fields">Only if you give it a forms file.</Card></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="s2" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="s2" class="t28">Stay safe</h2></div>
	<ul class="sets three"><li><div class="set mkr"><p>Run it on a staging app with test data, not on production.</p></div></li><li><div class="set mkr"><p>If you turn on probe-forms on a page you don’t own, you’re operating someone else's application.</p></div></li><li><div class="set mkr"><p>Never put real passwords or personal data in a forms file. It’s read as written, typed into a live page, and can appear in the transcript.</p></div></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="s3" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="s3" class="t28">What it sends</h2></div>
	<p>Nothing. It talks to the page you point it at and to your own machine. <span class="hl">There’s no tracking and no phoning home.</span></p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="s4" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="s4" class="t28">Report a problem privately</h2></div>
	<div class="set mkr" style="max-width:70ch"><p style="font-size:18px;color:var(--text)">If you find a security problem, use <a class="lnk2" href="https://github.com/a11ign/a11ign/security/advisories/new">GitHub's private vulnerability reporting</a>. Please don’t open a public issue for anything that could be abused. This is a small project, so we promise no response time, but we’ll read every report.</p></div>
	    </section></div>
	  </main>
</Page>

